+
+
+/// The structured-output shim as a shared library: g++ compiles it against xgrammar and links its
+/// C++ runtime statically, so the result has no libstdc++ dependency and needs no linker path.
+/// Zig loads it at run time (std.DynLib); a missing library leaves the engine without structured
+/// output instead of failing to link. Static linking through Zig's lld was not viable: the
+/// static libstdc++ archive is GCC-LTO, which lld cannot read.
+fn tfsoShared(b: *std.Build, target: std.Build.ResolvedTarget, xgrammar: []const u8) std.Build.LazyPath {
